# Beyond one NOT gate (task beyond-one-not; README items C4, T6). The plan and its five statements: notes/beyond-one-not.md.
# Rung 1 is the Theorem (at most one NOT gate, gates >= base, one open step). Here: the next rungs as conjectures,
# claimed on what exists and hunted with 2 and 3 NOT gates. A hunt that finds nothing proves nothing.
# Nothing here says anything about circuits of unbounded size or about P versus NP.

# --- S1  BoolSumNot 2 (and C4g(t)): t NOT gates save nothing.   Lean name of the statement: BoolSum.BoolSumNot t.
conjecture c4g: gates(c) >= base(c)
# --- S3  the count that would prove it: flip classes (gates whose value changes at two atoms of a set from a zero point,
#         counted once per function up to complement). flip classes <= gates, so fc implies c4g on the same circuit.
conjecture fc: margin["C4 count (flip classes)"](c) >= 0
# --- the old count (gates of any type, 0 at the zero point): refuted from 4 NOT gates, open at t = 2 and 3.
conjecture c4w: witness(c) >= base(c)

# The smallest system where a NOT gate could matter, as an OR tree: sets {0,1,2}, {0,3,4}, base 4.
# Exhaustive (one-not/tools/beyond_one_not/enum_small.c): no correct circuit with <= 3 gates, any number of NOT gates.
circuit twotri 5
  a = or 0 1
  b = or a 2
  d = or 0 3
  e = or d 4
  set 0 1 2 -> b
  set 0 3 4 -> e
end
claim correct(twotri) by lean
claim gates(twotri) = base(twotri)
claim c4g(twotri)
claim fc(twotri)

# Three NOT gates, none removable: x0 or x1 written as NOT(NOT x0 AND NOT x1). 9 gates = base + 3: the AND/OR gates alone
# are exactly base, so with NOT gates not counted the bound would still be tight. Found by experiments.py worlds 80 3 1.
circuit dm3 7
  a = not 0
  b = not 1
  k = and a b
  o = not k
  p = or o 2
  q = or 0 3
  r = or q 4
  s = or 0 5
  u = or s 6
  set 0 1 2 -> p
  set 0 3 4 -> r
  set 0 5 6 -> u
end
show dm3
claim correct(dm3) by lean
claim nots(dm3) = 3
claim gates(dm3) = 9
claim base(dm3) = 6
claim c4g(dm3)
claim fc(dm3)
claim witness(dm3) >= base(dm3) by lean
# WISH: claim gates(dm3) - nots(dm3) = base(dm3)     (arithmetic in terms: the AND/OR gate count, NOT gates free)
# WISH: claim faces(dm3) = 0                          (no assignment of constants to the NOT gates leaves a correct circuit)

# Two NOT gates, no constant face correct, no repeated function (hunted, not minimal): 11 gates against base 5.
let e2 = load one-not/data/beyond_one_not/essential_t2_seed1.json
claim correct(e2) by lean
claim nots(e2) = 2
claim c4g(e2)
claim fc(e2)
claim c4w(e2)

# The corpus by rung: at most 2, at most 3, any number of NOT gates (n <= 8).
corpus R2 = one-not/data/witnesses/*.json where n <= 8 where nots <= 2
corpus R3 = one-not/data/beyond_one_not/essential_t*.json where nots <= 3
corpus N = one-not/data/witnesses/nonlocal/general_count_below_base_*.json
claim forall c in R2: c4g(c)
claim forall c in R2: fc(c)
claim forall c in R3: c4g(c)
claim forall c in R3: fc(c)
claim forall c in R3: c4w(c)
claim forall c in N: c4g(c)
claim forall c in N: fc(c)
count c in N: witness(c) < base(c)
count c in R2: gates(c) = base(c)
# WISH: corpus ... where nots = T            (exactly T NOT gates; only an upper limit exists)
# WISH: savings(W, t) = max over c in W with nots(c) <= t of base(c) - gates(c)     (S2: the savings function f(t); 0 on everything seen)
# WISH: claim forall c in W: nots(c) <= 2 -> gates(c) >= base(c)                    (implication, as in theorem.ath)
# WISH: claim hyps(c) by lean                (hypsB with the NOT limit as a parameter t: today hypsB fixes "at most one NOT gate")
# WISH: a Lean form for c4g and for fc       (gates >= base and the flip-classes count have no kernel statement)
# WISH: claim forall sets forall zeros localflip(c) >= 0     (S3a, the per-set lemma: flip classes at one zero point of one set >= |S| - 1;
#                                                              a theorem for every t, proof in notes/beyond-one-not.md; tested in experiments.py local)
# WISH: worlds(c), live(c), forall worlds mslack(c, world)   (S5: the 2^t faces of a circuit with t NOT gates and the mixed slack of each face on its region)
# WISH: design(q) as a built-in system (projective plane of order q, n = q^2 + q + 1, base = n q) and hunt on it above n = 8   (S4)

# Hunts with 2 and 3 NOT gates (6 s each; starts: every circuit above with n <= 8 and its OR tree).
hunt c4g 6 2 1
hunt c4g 6 3 2
hunt fc 6 2 1
hunt fc 6 3 2
hunt c4w 6 3 1
